        "Do not fill unknown dimensions with zeros simply to produce a result. Use a reasonable category range only for early screening and mark it as assumed. Replace assumptions with warehouse measurements after items arrive and packaging choices are known. This is especially important for shoes with boxes, padded jackets, headwear that needs crush protection and multi-item parcels. A row should show whether its weight and dimensions are observed, seller-stated or estimated, because those are different levels of confidence."
