        "The practical lesson is simple: dense products and bulky products behave differently. Several lightweight boxes can create more chargeable volume than expected, while compact clothing may be closer to actual weight. Removing unnecessary seller packaging can reduce size, but protective packaging may prevent damage. Record the reason for each packaging request. Minimal packaging is not automatically best, and reinforced packaging is not automatically worth the added size. The right choice depends on fragility, replacement difficulty and the routes available to the destination."
